                 Design Document Front-End SafeVoice

Proposed changes to the SafeVoice front-end, prioritised with MoSCoW (Must, Should,
Could, Won’t), for feedback before implementation. Codes such as W1-06 refer to
ﬁndings in the Technical Plan.

User ﬂow:
Login page ó Topic overview ó Topic-speciﬁc record overview ó Record detail

From the topic overview the user can create a new topic, from the record overview the
user can add a new record to the topic, and from the record detail the user can submit a
correction.

General (all pages):                                                       Must
 Navigation menu to move between pages and back                            Must
 Logout button                                                             Must
 Clear error messages instead of technical error output                    Should
 Consistent layout and colour theme across all pages                       Should
 Short help text per ﬁeld explaining what to ﬁll in                        Could
 Usable on a mobile phone (small screen)

Login page:                                                                Must
 Fields for username and password                                          Must
 Error message when incorrect username and/or password                     Must
 Login replaces the manually typed Source ID; the user identity comes
 from the login (W3-01)                                                    Should
 Automatic logout after a period of inactivity                             Won’t
 Forgot username/password                                                  Won’t
 Legal Disclaimer

Topic overview:                                                            Must
 Only shows the user’s own topics (W3-02)                                  Must
 Shows per topic: title, creation date, number of records and last update  Must
 Topics sorted by most recent activity                                     Must
 Button to create a new topic                                              Should
 Search and ﬁlter topics

New topic:                                                                 Must
 Fields for title and short description                                    Must
 Automatically generated unique topic ID and creation date
Topic-speciﬁc record overview:                                              Must
 Only shows the user’s own records for this topic (W3-02)                   Must
 Shows per record: name, record ID, submission date and whether it has
 been corrected/updated                                                     Must
 Records sorted by submission date                                          Must
 Button to add a new record to this topic                                   Should
 Filter records on ﬁeld values (existing Manage Reports feature)

New record:                                                                 Must
 Narrative text box at the top                                              Must
 Structured ﬁelds below the narrative, grouped in collapsible sections
 (Incident, Victim, TraYicker, Publication)                                 Must
 Ability to name the record                                                 Must
 Automatically generated unique record ID that cannot be edited (W1-04)     Must
 Automatically generated submission timestamp                               Must
 Every ﬁeld empty by default, including drop-downs, coordinates and age,
 so no 0 or ﬁrst option is ﬁlled in (W1-06)                                 Must
 Required-ﬁelds checker that shows which ﬁelds are missing                  Must
 Input correctness checker: no dates in the future, departure date before
 arrival date, valid age, valid coordinates and valid URLs                  Must
 Conﬁrmation step before submitting                                         Must
 Feedback after submitting: a success message or a clear error message      Should
 Upload documents (prototype: dummy ﬁles only)                              Could
 Save as draft, so a long narrative is not lost when the page is refreshed  Won’t
 Automated information extraction from the narrative using an encoder
 on narrative box like BERT

Record detail:                                                              Must
 Read-only view of a submitted record                                       Must
 Shows the cleaned data, not the raw input with exact coordinates (W4-
 02)                                                                        Must
 Button to submit a correction                                              Must
 Shows the correction history: the original record and its linked
 corrections (GitHub like)                                                  Should
 Shows attached documents

Submit correction:                                                          Must
 Form pre-ﬁlled with the data of the record being corrected                 Must
 Correction is saved as a new record linked to the original; the original
 stays unchanged                                                            Should
 Field for the reason of the correction

Open questions:
1. Is a record only owned by one user, or should they be able to share a record?
2. Are there other roles, for example an aid-organization who can see all topics and
records?
3. Which ﬁelds should a topic have besides a title and description?
4. What is the minimum information required to submit a record?
5. What may be corrected, and when should a new record be made or the previous
deleted?
6. Will users use the application on a mobile phone?
7. Which types of documents need to be uploaded?
